230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (WMI Microfinance stands as a compelling example of how community-driven lending models can succeed where conventional financial institutions often fail. By relying on trust, peer monitoring, and social cohesion, WMI has consistently achieved repayment rates of over 97%, even in rural markets where traditional collateral is scarce and credit risk is typically high. This highlights the enduring value of social capital as a foundation for financial inclusion.)
/Pg 21 0 R
>>
endobj
