endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Additional priorities will be critical to sustaining repayment culture in a rapidly changing rural economy. These include funding diversification to reduce dependence on a narrow donor base, financial literacy programs to equip borrowers for digital transition, and borrower-centric innovations such as flexible repayment schedules that align with agricultural income cycles. Together, these measures reduce systemic risk and enhance institutional resilience.)
/Pg 21 0 R
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (With these steps, WMI can transform itself into a model for small MFIs seeking to scale without losing their core strengths. By combining grassroots trust with digital efficiency, the institution not only ensures its own sustainability but also contributes to a broader vision of inclusive, resilient, and scalable rural finance. This balance positions WMI as both a practitioner and a thought leader in the next generation of financial inclusion models.)
/Pg 21 0 R
>>
endobj
